# Contracts, evidence, time, persistence

Start with `docs/implementation/agent_reference_index.md`, then follow the Phase 010 Group 02 / active implementation references it names.

Preserve directly:

- canonical identity/reference IDs are distinct from source-local IDs;
- Observation/evidence is not Assessment or truth-by-arrival;
- event/effective time, source availability, collection/persistence, framework knowledge/recorded time, derived evaluation, correction/supersession, and communication time remain distinct where material;
- current retrieval of an old fact does not backdate framework knowledge;
- later evidence cannot appear in an earlier `known by K` cut;
- correction/supersession appends/links state and preserves what was previously recorded;
- missing/restricted/failed/unavailable evidence is not negative truth;
- negative claims require bounded opportunity-to-observe and sufficient coverage;
- Delta time travel is not the sole product definition of historical/as-known replay;
- persistence/storage maintenance must not rewrite semantic history.

Use stable REF/ARCH tags in tests and ADRs. Prefer opaque typed IDs and explicit temporal types over generic strings/timestamps.
